    "Folded from 44 one-function sources (func_ov004_020b2c84 .. func_ov004_020b4aa0). func_ov004_020b2cb8 had no complete delinks entry before, but it byte-matched; what it lacked was a licence for the 0xe8-byte table its local array initializer copies from. A local `Entry entries[29] = {...}` makes mwccarm emit that table as an anonymous input .rodata object (@N), while the cartridge keeps it in the module's .data at 0x020bc6e8, which the intact-object link cannot place from .rodata. The unit therefore defines it as an ordinary initialized global under its configured name data_ov004_020bc6e8, and the function copies it with a plain struct copy; the emitted instructions are the same.",
    "`#pragma defer_codegen off` is load-bearing: the shards' file-global opt_strength_reduction (func_ov004_020b2cb8) and opt_propagation (func_ov004_020b3b38, func_ov004_020b4360, func_ov004_020b45c0) pragmas bind to their one function only with undeferred codegen, which also makes the source ROM-ascending.",
    "The per-source extern declarations disagreed on type for several symbols (data_ov004_020bf560 and data_ov006_021346bc as int vs pointer, func_ov004_020b1cf0's argument widths, func_ov004_020b39a4's return type); the single declaration set in the unit source picks one spelling each and the bodies cast to match. func_ov004_020b3c58 became void: no caller uses a result, and the void body compiles to the same bytes.",
